# ── AI CoAudS — Docker build-context filter ──────────────────────────────
# CRITICAL: the web bundle inlines repo files at build time via Vite ?raw
# imports (src/data/codebase.ts + the README import in Readme.tsx). These
# paths MUST remain in the context or `npm run build` fails inside Docker:
#
#   backend/**  deploy/**  .github/workflows/**  docker-compose.yml  README.md
#
# Only exclude paths proven unused at build time. Patterns that could match
# a same-named file deeper in the tree are anchored with a leading "/" —
# e.g. unanchored `.env.*` would also swallow backend/.env.example, which
# IS a ?raw import.

node_modules
dist
.git
*.log
/.env
/.env.*
